---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="How This Works"
	description="How the agentic build workflow works, from setup to launch."
	noindex
>
	<section class="container section">
		<h1>How this site gets built</h1>
		<p class="intro">
			This page exists to walk through the workflow live with a client — not
			for public search. It's marked <code>noindex</code> so it never shows up
			in Google.
		</p>

		<h2>1. The workflow, in one paragraph</h2>
		<p>
			Instead of a visual page builder, this site is built with <strong>Claude
			Code</strong>: you describe what you want in plain English &mdash; "add a
			testimonials section," "change the phone number in the footer" &mdash;
			and it writes the actual code, checks it, and can publish it live. There's
			no drag-and-drop editor to learn.
		</p>

		<h2>2. Who owns what</h2>
		<p>
			You own the site from day one. Two free accounts, both in your name:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>GitHub</strong> &mdash; where the site's code lives.</li>
			<li><strong>Vercel</strong> &mdash; where the site is actually hosted/published.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Your developer is added as a collaborator on GitHub, not given your
			login. Nothing about your site depends on their account existing.
		</p>

		<h2>3. One-time setup (about 10 minutes)</h2>
		<ol>
			<li>Create a free GitHub account.</li>
			<li>Create a new repository from this starter template.</li>
			<li>Add your developer as a collaborator on that repository.</li>
			<li>Create a free Vercel account and import that GitHub repository &mdash; Vercel auto-deploys it.</li>
			<li>Confirm Deployment Protection is off, so preview links work without logging in.</li>
		</ol>
		<p>That's the entire setup. After this, changes just get pushed and go live automatically.</p>

		<h2>4. Day-to-day, once it's live</h2>
		<p>
			Most updates happen through your developer: you describe the change, they
			(or Claude Code directly) make it, it deploys automatically. If you ever
			want to make small text/content changes yourself, you can talk to Claude
			Code directly the same way &mdash; there's no separate login or dashboard
			to learn beyond what's already set up above.
		</p>

		<h2>5. Extra pieces, added only if needed</h2>
		<p>Each of these is optional and only gets added if the site actually needs it &mdash; fewer accounts is better:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Forms</strong> &mdash; Formspree (free), submissions go straight to your inbox.</li>
			<li><strong>Scheduling</strong> &mdash; Calendly or Cal.com (free), booking on your own calendar.</li>
			<li><strong>Payments</strong> &mdash; Stripe Payment Links, money goes straight to your Stripe account.</li>
			<li><strong>Photo galleries updated often</strong> &mdash; either a simple GitHub upload (a few clicks, no new account) or a dedicated image host if updates are frequent.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>6. What this is not</h2>
		<p>
			This isn't a monthly-fee website builder. There's no platform subscription
			&mdash; just free hosting accounts plus whatever third-party service (if
			any) a specific feature needs.
		</p>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.section {
		padding-block: var(--space-2xl);
		max-width: 720px;
	}

	.intro {
		font-size: var(--text-h3);
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
	}

	li {
		margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
	}
</style>
